CORE gcc-only
main.c
--pointer-check --bounds-check
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ reachable after a false alignment claim: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The model returns its first argument, also for a pointer to const and in the
three-argument form, and neither assumes nor checks the alignment claim: the
final assertion must be reachable.
